1
00:00:00,097 --> 00:00:01,227
(Leonard's Mother:)Oh.

2
00:00:01,390 --> 00:00:02,520
(Beverley:)Your Uncle Floyd died.

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,140
(Leonard:)Oh, my God. What happened?

4
00:00:05,310 --> 00:00:07,400
(Beverley:)His heart stopped beating.

5
00:00:08,605 --> 00:00:09,815
(Beverley:)I have to urinate.

6
00:00:15,654 --> 00:00:18,364
(Sheldon:)What a remarkable woman.

7
00:00:19,783 --> 00:00:22,823
(Leonard:)Yeah, I... I thought
you guys might hit it off.

8
00:00:22,995 --> 00:00:24,915
(Sheldon:)I envy you your childhood.

9
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,290
(Leonard:)I hate to tell you...

10
00:00:26,457 --> 00:00:31,337
(Leonard:)...but the only warm memories I have
of my childhood are of my Uncle Floyd.

11
00:00:31,503 --> 00:00:35,673
(Sheldon:)You're clearly misremembering. Your mother
is brilliant, analytical, insightful.

12
00:00:35,841 --> 00:00:40,011
(Sheldon:)I'm betting she never hit you with a Bible
because you wouldn't eat Brussels sprouts.

13
00:00:40,804 --> 00:00:43,344
(Leonard:)Sheldon, you don't give
your mother enough credit.

14
00:00:43,515 --> 00:00:47,055
(Leonard:)She's warm, she's loving,
she doesn't glue electrodes to your head...

15
00:00:47,227 --> 00:00:50,437
(Leonard:)...to measure your brain waves
while potty training.

16
00:00:51,064 --> 00:00:52,194
(Sheldon:)You were lucky.

17
00:00:52,357 --> 00:00:59,027
(Sheldon:)When I was a kid, if I wanted an EEG,
I had to attach my own electrodes.

